WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.339
All together: Good morning.

2
00:00:01.639 --> 00:00:08.660
We’re Ona, Adam, Iker and Mariam, and we’d like to convince you that our school should hold a Lucia Morning.

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.537
Ona: St Lucia’s Day, on the thirteenth of December, has two roots.

4
00:00:13.837 --> 00:00:22.235
One is religious: Lucy was a Christian woman from Syracuse, in Sicily, who was killed for her faith in the year 304.

5
00:00:22.535 --> 00:00:31.971
The other is a folk tradition: in the old calendar, this was the longest night of the year in Sweden, and people used to stay awake to keep the darkness away.

6
00:00:32.271 --> 00:00:42.217
Although it began as a saint’s day, for most Swedes today it is a cultural tradition about light and community, which is why it suits a school with many different beliefs.

7
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.479
Adam: I’m Adam.

8
00:00:44.779 --> 00:00:47.152
Lucia has changed a lot over time.

9
00:00:47.452 --> 00:01:00.443
It used to be a family custom on farms in western Sweden, but in 1927 Stockholm held its first public Lucia, and the tradition spread to schools across the country.

10
00:01:00.743 --> 00:01:07.827
Real candles have been replaced by battery ones for safety, and the morning concert is now on television.

11
00:01:08.127 --> 00:01:21.286
Here in Catalonia, Santa Llúcia falls on the same day; however, it is mainly known for Barcelona’s Christmas fair, which has been held since 1786.

12
00:01:21.586 --> 00:01:26.082
So while Swedes sing about light, we buy figures for the nativity scene.

13
00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.172
Iker: I’m Iker.

14
00:01:28.472 --> 00:01:34.194
Our Lucia Morning will be on Friday the eleventh of December, as the thirteenth falls on a Sunday.

15
00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:40.968
At a quarter to nine, the lights will go off and the procession will walk through the corridors, so every class can see it.

16
00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:46.706
Ona will coordinate the volunteers, and Adam will prepare the song with the music department.

17
00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:57.470
From a quarter to ten, I’ll run three workshops with 1st ESO, and Mariam will organise a “fika” at break time, followed by a quiz comparing Lucia and Santa Llúcia.

18
00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.551
Mariam: I’m Mariam.

19
00:01:59.851 --> 00:02:05.071
Our materials will cost about seventy euros, while the white T-shirts will come from home.

20
00:02:05.371 --> 00:02:15.152
The procession is voluntary, so whoever prefers not to walk can help backstage, and we’ll offer buns without gluten or eggs, so nobody is left out.

21
00:02:15.452 --> 00:02:20.294
Most importantly, Lucia will be chosen by lottery from all the volunteers.

22
00:02:20.594 --> 00:02:30.842
Some people believe Lucia has to be a blonde girl; however, Sweden is a diverse country, and our research showed that in many schools any child can be Lucia.

23
00:02:31.143 --> 00:02:33.913
Our lottery challenges that idea directly.

24
00:02:34.213 --> 00:02:34.921
Thank you.
